Scala is a programming language that is primarily used for building software applications. While it is possible to write code that generates text, it is not the best tool for creating a comprehensive declaration of an organization's purpose, objectives, and values.
However, you can use Scala to build software applications that are designed to help organizations manage their mission statements and other organizational documents. For example, you can build a web application that allows users to create, edit, and share their organization's mission statement. Here is an example of Scala code that can be used to create a web application that allows users to create and edit a mission statement:
```
import akka.actor.ActorSystem
import akka.http.scaladsl.Http
import akka.http.scaladsl.server.Directives._
import akka.stream.ActorMaterializer
object MissionStatementApp extends App {
  implicit val system = ActorSystem("mission-statement-app")
  implicit val materializer = ActorMaterializer()
  implicit val executionContext = system.dispatcher
  val routes = path("mission-statement") {
    get {
      complete("This is our mission statement.")
    } ~
    post {
      entity(as[String]) { missionStatement =>
        complete(s"Mission statement updated to: $missionStatement")
      }
    }
  }
  val bindingFuture = Http().bindAndHandle(routes, "localhost", 8080)
  println(s"Server online at http://localhost:8080/\nPress Ctrl+C to stop...")
}
```
This code creates a web server that listens for HTTP requests on port 8080. When a GET request is received for the path "/mission-statement", the server responds with a default mission statement. When a POST request is received for the same path, the server updates the mission statement with the new value provided in the request body and responds with a confirmation message.
Of course, this is just a simple example, and a real-world mission statement application would likely require more complex functionality and user interfaces. But this should give you an idea of how Scala can be used to build software applications that help organizations manage their mission statements and other organizational documents.

