To store the user-provided length and width values in a SQL database, you will need to create a table in the database with "length" and "width" columns to store the values. Here is an example of how you can create a "rectangle" table in the database:
```SQL
CREATE TABLE rectangle (
    id INT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
    length FLOAT,
    width FLOAT
);
```
To connect to the SQL database in Swift, you can use a library like SwiftMySQL. Here is an example of how you can connect to the database:
```Swift
