Sure, here's the PHP code that converts the sentence "She likes to dance" into present progressive tense and also checks for gender-neutral pronouns:
```
$sentence = "She likes to dance";
$words = explode(" ", $sentence);
// Check for gender-neutral pronouns
foreach($words as $word) {
  if($word == "they" || $word == "them" || $word == "their") {
    $pronoun = "They";
    break;
  } elseif($word == "he" || $word == "him" || $word == "his") {
    $pronoun = "He";
    break;
  } elseif($word == "she" || $word == "her" || $word == "hers") {
    $pronoun = "She";
    break;
  }
}
// Convert sentence to present progressive tense
if(isset($pronoun)) {
  $sentence = str_replace($pronoun, $pronoun . " are", $sentence);
} else {
  $sentence = str_replace("likes", "is liking", $sentence);
}
echo $sentence;
```
This code first checks for gender-neutral pronouns in the sentence using a foreach loop and sets the appropriate pronoun variable. It then uses the str_replace function to convert the sentence to present progressive tense by replacing "likes" with "is liking" or "are" depending on the pronoun variable. Finally, it echoes the converted sentence.

