How can I use Java to develop a web application that allows users to search for books based on specific criteria, such as author, title, and genre?
Assuming that the web application will connect to a database of books, you can use Java to create a search functionality that queries the database based on user input. Here is an example Java code that demonstrates how to connect to a MySQL database and execute a search query:
```
import java.sql.*;
public class BookSearch {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String url = "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/books";
        String user = "root";
        String password = "password";
        try {
            Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(url, user, password);
            System.out.println("Database connected successfully!");
            String searchAuthor = "Stephen King";
            String searchTitle = "The Shining";
            String searchGenre = "Horror";
            String query = "SELECT * FROM books WHERE author = ? AND title = ? AND genre = ?";
            PreparedStatement statement = connection.prepareStatement(query);
            statement.setString(1, searchAuthor);
            statement.setString(2, searchTitle);
            statement.setString(3, searchGenre);
            ResultSet resultSet = statement.executeQuery();
            while(resultSet.next()) {
                int id = resultSet.getInt("id");
                String author = resultSet.getString("author");
                String title = resultSet.getString("title");
                String genre = resultSet.getString("genre");
                System.out.println(id + ", " + author + ", " + title + ", " + genre);
            }
            statement.close();
            connection.close();
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            System.out.println("Error connecting to database: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```
This code connects to a MySQL database with the URL "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/books", using the username "root" and password "password". It then executes a search query that selects all books where the author, title, and genre match the user's search criteria. The search criteria in this example are hard-coded as "Stephen King" for the author, "The Shining" for the title, and "Horror" for the genre, but these could be replaced with user input from a web form. The results of the query are printed to the console. 
