To implement a timer system in C# that triggers a message after a certain amount of time has passed, you can use the `System.Timers.Timer` class. Here's an example of how you can use this class to display a message to the runners advising them to pick up the pace:
```csharp
using System;
using System.Timers;
class Program
{
    static Timer timer;
    static int timeLimit = 60; // time limit in seconds
    static int elapsedTime = 0;
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        timer = new Timer(1000); // create a timer that ticks every second
        timer.Elapsed += OnTimerElapsed; // register the OnTimerElapsed method as the event handler for the Elapsed event
        timer.Start(); // start the timer
        Console.WriteLine("The race has started. You have {0} seconds to complete it.", timeLimit);
        Console.ReadLine();
    }
    static void OnTimerElapsed(object sender, ElapsedEventArgs e)
    {
        elapsedTime++;
        if (elapsedTime >= timeLimit)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Time's up! You didn't finish the race within the time limit.");
            timer.Stop();
        }
        else if (elapsedTime >= timeLimit * 0.8)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("You're falling behind schedule. Pick up the pace!");
        }
    }
}
```
In this example, we create a `Timer` object that ticks every second (`1000` milliseconds). We also define a `timeLimit` variable that represents the time limit in seconds, and an `elapsedTime` variable that keeps track of how much time has passed since the race started.
In the `Main` method, we start the timer and display a message to the runners advising them of the time limit.
In the `OnTimerElapsed` method, we increment the `elapsedTime` variable and check if it has exceeded the `timeLimit`. If it has, we display a message indicating that the race is over. If the `elapsedTime` is greater than or equal to 80% of the `timeLimit`, we display a message advising the runners to pick up the pace.
Once the `elapsedTime` exceeds the `timeLimit`, we stop the timer using the `Stop` method.

